// THE BOOK OF THE SECRETS OF ENOCH (2 ENOCH), CHAPTERS I–LXVIII, IN PLAIN
// WORDS: a close paraphrase of each verse of W. R. Morfill's English as R. H.
// Charles formed the text (Oxford, 1896), translated from the Slavonic. Three
// voices are kept apart, as the text keeps them: the narrator, who speaks of
// Enoch in the third person (the prologue, the opening words of i. 1 'At that
// time he said', lvi–lvii, lxiv and lxvii–lxviii)
// ("The narrator says ..."); Enoch, who tells of his ascent and his return and
// instructs his sons in the first person (i–xxiii, xxxvii–lv, lviii–lxvi)
// ("Enoch says ..."); and the Lord, whose long speech to Enoch Enoch reports
// (xxiv. 2–xxxvi) ("The Lord says ..."). Methosalem's few words are reported
// by the narrator. Nothing here is offered as an account of real events: it
// is what the text says. Words in Charles's square brackets (A's chapter
// titles, and later additions) are left out of the paraphrase of the verse,
// except where the brackets enclose verse text, which is paraphrased and said
// to be bracketed. Charles's footnotes were not imported and are not
// reported, save where the work's notes give one.

export const PLAIN_SECRETS_OF_ENOCH: Record<string, string> = {
  "gnostic.2en.prologue":
    "The narrator says that this is the book of the secrets of Enoch, son of Ared, a wise man whom God loved. There was a very wise man who did great things. God loved him and took him up so that he could see the dwellings of heaven, the kingdoms of the wise and unchanging God, the Lord of all; the bright place where the Lord's servants stand; the Lord's throne, which no one can approach; the ranks and appearances of the bodiless hosts; the service of the multitude of creatures; and the singing of the Cherubim, which no one can describe, and the world that cannot be measured.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- I
  "gnostic.2en.1.1":
    "The narrator says that at that time Enoch said: when he was barely 165 years old his son Methusal was born; after that he lived another 200 years, 365 years in all.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.2": "Enoch says that on the first day of the first month he was alone in his house, and lay down on his bed and fell asleep.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.3":
    "Enoch says that as he slept a great grief came over his heart and he wept in his dream, and he could not understand what the grief meant or what would happen to him.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.4": "Enoch says that two very tall men appeared to him, men such as he had never seen on earth.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.5":
    "Enoch says that their faces shone like the sun, their eyes were like burning lamps, and fire came out of their lips; their clothing looked like feathers, their feet were purple, their wings brighter than gold and their hands whiter than snow. They stood at the head of his bed and called him by name.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.6": "Enoch says that he woke up and saw the men clearly, standing in front of him.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.7": "Enoch says that he quickly bowed down to them, terrified, and his face changed with fear.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.8":
    "Enoch says that the men told him: 'Take heart, Enoch, do not be afraid. The everlasting God has sent us to you, and today you will go up with us into heaven.",
  "gnostic.2en.1.9":
    "Enoch goes on with the men's words: 'Tell your sons and all the servants of your house, and let no one look for you until the Lord brings you back to them.'",
  "gnostic.2en.1.10":
    "Enoch says that he hurried to obey them and went out of his house, called his sons Methusal, Regim and Gaidal (Gaidal's name is in square brackets), and told them the wonderful things the two men had said.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- II
  "gnostic.2en.2.1": "Enoch says to his children: 'Listen to me, for I do not know where I am going or what is waiting for me.'",
  "gnostic.2en.2.2":
    "Enoch tells his children not to turn away from God, to walk before the Lord and keep his judgements, and not to worship empty gods who did not make heaven and earth: those gods will perish, and so will those who worship them.",
  "gnostic.2en.2.3": "Enoch says: 'May God make your hearts confident in the fear of him.'",
  "gnostic.2en.2.4": "Enoch tells his children that no one is to look for him until the Lord brings him back to them.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- III
  "gnostic.2en.3.1":
    "Enoch says that when he had spoken to his sons, the men called him, took him on their wings and set him on the clouds, and the clouds moved.",
  "gnostic.2en.3.2": "Enoch says that going higher he saw the air, and higher still the ether, and they set him down in the first heaven.",
  "gnostic.2en.3.3": "Enoch says that they showed him a very great sea, greater than the sea on earth.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- IV
  "gnostic.2en.4.1":
    "Enoch says that they brought before him the elders and the rulers of the orders of the stars, and showed him the two hundred angels who rule the stars and their service in heaven.",
  "gnostic.2en.4.2": "Enoch says that these angels fly with their wings and go round all the stars as they float.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- V
  "gnostic.2en.5.1": "Enoch says that he saw the storehouses of snow and ice, and the angels who guard their terrible stores,",
  "gnostic.2en.5.2": "Enoch goes on: and the storehouses of the clouds, from which they come out and into which they go back.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- VI
  "gnostic.2en.6.1":
    "Enoch says that they showed him the storehouses of the dew, which is like oil for anointing and looks like every colour on earth, and many angels who keep these stores, shutting and opening them.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- VII
  "gnostic.2en.7.1":
    "Enoch says that the men brought him to the second heaven and showed him darkness, and there he saw prisoners hanging, held for the eternal judgement and waiting for it.",
  "gnostic.2en.7.2":
    "Enoch says that these angels looked gloomier than the darkness on earth and wept without ceasing, every hour; he asked the men why they were tortured all the time.",
  "gnostic.2en.7.3":
    "Enoch says the men answered that these are the ones who turned away from the Lord: they did not obey God's commandments but followed their own will, rebelled together with their prince, and are already shut up in the second heaven.",
  "gnostic.2en.7.4": "Enoch says that he felt great pity for them, and the angels bowed down to him and asked him, as a man of God, to pray to the Lord for them.",
  "gnostic.2en.7.5":
    "Enoch says that he answered them: 'Who am I, a mortal man, to pray for angels? Who knows where I am going, or what is waiting for me, or who prays for me?'",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- VIII
  "gnostic.2en.8.1":
    "Enoch says that the men took him from there to the third heaven and set him in the middle of a garden, a place more beautiful than any ever known.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.2": "Enoch says that he saw trees of beautiful colours, with ripe and fragrant fruit, and every kind of food they bore, giving off a delightful scent.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.3":
    "Enoch says that in the middle is the tree of life, in the place where God rests when he comes into Paradise; the tree cannot be described, it is so excellent and so sweet-smelling.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.4": "Enoch says that it is more beautiful than anything created; on every side it looks like gold and crimson and is as transparent as fire, and it covers everything.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.5": "Enoch says that from its root in the garden four streams go out, pouring honey and milk, oil and wine; they part in four directions and flow gently round.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.6":
    "Enoch says that they go down to the Paradise of Eden, between what decays and what does not decay, and from there go along the earth, turning in their circle like the other elements.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.7": "Enoch says that there is another tree, an olive tree always dripping oil; there is no tree there without fruit, and every tree is blessed.",
  "gnostic.2en.8.8":
    "Enoch says that three hundred very glorious angels keep the garden and serve the Lord every day with never-ceasing voices and blessed singing. He said, 'What a blessed place this is!', and the men answered him.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- IX
  "gnostic.2en.9.1":
    "Enoch says the men told him that this place is prepared for the righteous, as their eternal inheritance: those who endure every kind of attack in their lives from people who afflict them; who turn their eyes from wrongdoing and judge rightly; who give bread to the hungry, clothe the naked, lift up the fallen and help oppressed orphans; and who walk blamelessly before the Lord and serve him alone.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- X
  "gnostic.2en.10.1": "Enoch says that the men then took him to the northern region and showed him a very terrible place.",
  "gnostic.2en.10.2":
    "Enoch says that every kind of torture is there: savage darkness and gloom that nothing can pierce, no light but a gloomy fire always burning, and a fiery river flowing out. Fire is on every side of the place, and cold and ice on every side, so that it both burns and freezes.",
  "gnostic.2en.10.3": "Enoch says that the prisoners are very savage, and the angels are terrible and pitiless, carrying savage weapons, and their torture is merciless.",
  "gnostic.2en.10.4":
    "Enoch says that he cried out at how terrible the place was, and the men told him it is prepared for those who do not honour God: who do evil on earth, sodomy (the English leaves the phrase in Latin), witchcraft, enchantments and devilish magic, who boast of their evil, and who steal, lie, slander, envy, think evil, commit fornication and murder.",
  "gnostic.2en.10.5":
    "Enoch goes on with the men's words: those who steal the souls of wretched people, oppress the poor and rob them, and grow rich by taking and harming what belongs to others; who could feed the hungry but let them starve, and could clothe them but strip them naked.",
  "gnostic.2en.10.6":
    "Enoch goes on with the men's words: those who do not know their Creator and worship lifeless gods that can neither see nor hear, who make idols and bow down to worthless things made by hands. For all of these this place is prepared as an eternal inheritance.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XI
  "gnostic.2en.11.1":
    "Enoch says that the men took him to the fourth heaven and showed him all the comings and goings and all the rays of the light of the sun and moon; he measured their courses and reckoned their light.",
  "gnostic.2en.11.2":
    "Enoch says that the sun's light is seven times greater than the moon's; he saw their circle and the chariot on which each goes like a wind, astonishingly fast, never resting day or night, coming or going.",
  "gnostic.2en.11.3":
    "Enoch says that there are four great stars at the right of the sun's chariot, each with a thousand stars under it, and four at the left, each with a thousand under it, eight thousand in all.",
  "gnostic.2en.11.4":
    "Enoch says that a hundred and fifty thousand angels go out with the sun and attend him by day, and a thousand by night; each angel has six wings, and they go before the sun's chariot.",
  "gnostic.2en.11.5": "Enoch says that a hundred angels keep the sun warm and light him up.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XII
  "gnostic.2en.12.1":
    "Enoch says that he saw other flying creatures called phoenixes and chalkadri, wonderful and strange, with the feet and tails of lions and the heads of crocodiles; they were purple, like the rainbow, and nine hundred measures in size.",
  "gnostic.2en.12.2": "Enoch says that their wings were like angels' wings, twelve each; they attend the sun's chariot and go with him, bringing heat and dew as God orders them.",
  "gnostic.2en.12.3": "Enoch says that so the sun goes round, passing under the heavens and under the earth, with the light of his rays never ceasing.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XIII
  "gnostic.2en.13.1":
    "Enoch says that the men brought him to the east and showed him the gates by which the sun goes out at the set seasons, following the round of the months of the whole year and the number of the hours of day and night.",
  "gnostic.2en.13.2":
    "Enoch says that he saw six great gates standing open, each sixty-one and a quarter stadia wide; he measured them carefully and found them that size. Through them the sun goes out and travels to the west, keeping his course in step, and goes through all the months.",
  "gnostic.2en.13.3":
    "Enoch says that the sun goes out by the first gates for forty-two days, by the second for thirty-five, by the fourth for thirty-five, by the fifth for thirty-five, and by the sixth for forty-five. (The third gates are not mentioned in this verse.)",
  "gnostic.2en.13.4":
    "Enoch says that then the sun comes back from the sixth gates in due time and goes in by the fifth gates for thirty-five days, by the fourth for thirty-five, by the third for thirty-five, and by the second for thirty-five.",
  "gnostic.2en.13.5": "Enoch says that so the days of the whole year are completed, as the four seasons follow one another.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XIV
  "gnostic.2en.14.1":
    "Enoch says that the men took him to the west of the heavens and showed him six great gates standing open, matching the eastern gates by which the sun goes out, according to the number of days, 365 and a quarter.",
  "gnostic.2en.14.2": "Enoch says that the sun sets by the western gates, and when he goes out by them four hundred angels take his crown and bring it to the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.14.3":
    "Enoch says that the sun turns round in his chariot and travels without light for seven full hours of the night; at the eighth hour of the night, when he comes near the east, the four hundred angels bring his crown and crown him.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XV
  "gnostic.2en.15.1":
    "Enoch says that then the creatures called the Phoenixes and the Chalkidri sang, so that every bird claps its wings, rejoicing at the giver of light, and they sang a song at the Lord's command.",
  "gnostic.2en.15.2": "Enoch says that the giver of light comes to give his brightness to the whole world.",
  "gnostic.2en.15.3": "Enoch says that they showed him how the sun's course is reckoned; the gates by which he goes in and out are great gates that God made for counting the year.",
  "gnostic.2en.15.4": "Enoch says that this is why the sun is great.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XVI
  "gnostic.2en.16.1":
    "Enoch says that the men also showed him the reckoning of the moon, all her courses and revolutions, and pointed out twelve great gates stretching from west to east, by which the moon goes in and out at the usual times.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.2":
    "Enoch says that she goes in by the first gate, when the sun is in the west, for exactly thirty-one days; by the second, thirty-one; the third, thirty; the fourth, thirty; the fifth, thirty-one; the sixth, thirty-one; the seventh, thirty; the eighth, thirty-one; the ninth, thirty-one; the tenth, thirty; the eleventh, thirty-one; and the twelfth, twenty-eight.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.3": "Enoch says that in the same way she goes round by the western gates, matching the number of the eastern gates, and completes the year.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.4": "Enoch says that the sun has 365 and a quarter days.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.5":
    "Enoch says that the lunar year has 354 days, twelve months of twenty-nine days, and eleven days are left over, which belong to the sun's circle of the whole year and are the lunar epacts of the year. A last sentence, in square brackets, adds that the great circle is 532 years.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.6":
    "Enoch says that the quarter of a day is left out for three years and the fourth year makes it up exactly; so for three years these quarters are left out of the heavens and not added to the count of days, and for this reason they change the seasons of the year, two new months making the number complete and two others diminishing it.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.7":
    "Enoch says that when the moon has gone through the western gates she comes back to the eastern with her light, going day and night in the heavenly circles, below all the circles and faster than the winds of heaven; and spirits, creatures and angels fly there, each angel with six wings.",
  "gnostic.2en.16.8": "Enoch says that seven months are added to the moon's circle in a cycle of nineteen years.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XVII
  "gnostic.2en.17.1": "Enoch says that in the middle of the heavens he saw an armed host serving the Lord with cymbals, organs and unceasing voice, and he was delighted to hear it.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XVIII
  "gnostic.2en.18.1":
    "Enoch says that the men brought him up to the fifth heaven, where he saw countless hosts called Grigori; they looked like men but were bigger than the giants.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.2":
    "Enoch says that their faces were withered and their lips always silent, and there was no service in the fifth heaven; he asked the men why they were so withered, sad-faced and silent, and why there was no service there.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.3": "Enoch says the men answered that these are the Grigori, who with their prince Satanail rejected the holy Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.4":
    "Enoch goes on with the men's words: because of this their fellows are held in great darkness in the second heaven; and three of them went down to the earth from God's throne, to the place Ermon, and on the side of Mount Iermon they saw that the daughters of men were beautiful and took wives from them.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.5": "Enoch goes on with the men's words: they fouled the earth with their deeds, acted lawlessly all through that age and caused confusion; the giants were born, and strangely tall men, and there was much wickedness.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.6": "Enoch goes on with the men's words: so God judged them with a mighty judgement; and these Grigori mourn for their brothers, and they will be punished on the great day of the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.7":
    "Enoch says that he told the Grigori that he had seen their brothers, their deeds and their great torments, and had prayed for them, but God has condemned them to be under the earth until heaven and earth end for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.8": "Enoch says that he asked them why they were waiting and did not serve before the Lord, and told them to do their duties before him and not to anger him for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.18.9":
    "Enoch says that they heeded his rebuke and stood in four ranks in that heaven; and as he stood with the men, four trumpets sounded together loudly, and the Grigori sang with one voice, and their voices rose before the Lord, sad and tender.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XIX
  "gnostic.2en.19.1":
    "Enoch says that the men took him to the sixth heaven, where he saw seven bands of angels, very bright and glorious, their faces shining more than the sun's rays; they were radiant, and there was no difference between them in face, manner or clothing.",
  "gnostic.2en.19.2": "Enoch says that these orders arrange and study the courses of the stars, the changes of the moon and the courses of the sun, and oversee the good or bad state of the world.",
  "gnostic.2en.19.3":
    "Enoch says that they arrange teachings and instructions, sweet speaking, singing and every kind of glorious praise. These are the archangels set over the angels, and they hold every living thing in heaven and earth subject to them.",
  "gnostic.2en.19.4":
    "Enoch says that there are angels over the seasons and years, over rivers and the sea, over the fruits of the earth and over every plant, giving every kind of food to every living thing.",
  "gnostic.2en.19.5": "Enoch says that there are angels over all the souls of men, who write down all their deeds and their lives before the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.19.6":
    "Enoch says that among them are seven phoenixes, seven cherubim and seven six-winged creatures, singing with one voice; their singing cannot be described, and they rejoice before the Lord at his footstool.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XX
  "gnostic.2en.20.1":
    "Enoch says that the men took him to the seventh heaven, where he saw a very great light and all the fiery hosts of great archangels, bodiless powers, lordships, principalities and powers, cherubim and seraphim, thrones and the watchfulness of many eyes: ten troops, a place of brightness. He was afraid and trembled with great terror.",
  "gnostic.2en.20.2": "Enoch says that the men took hold of him, brought him into their midst and told him to take heart and not be afraid.",
  "gnostic.2en.20.3": "Enoch says that they showed him the Lord far off, sitting on his high throne; all the hosts of heaven came near, stood on the ten steps according to their rank, and bowed down to the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.20.4": "Enoch says that then they went to their places in joy and gladness, in boundless light, singing with low and gentle voices and serving him gloriously.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXI
  "gnostic.2en.21.1":
    "Enoch says that the cherubim and seraphim never leave the Lord's presence day or night but stand round his throne doing his will, and the six-winged creatures cover the whole throne, singing softly before the Lord: 'Holy, holy, holy, Lord God of Sabaoth, heaven and earth are full of your glory!'",
  "gnostic.2en.21.2":
    "Enoch says that when he had seen all this, the men told him that they had been ordered to go with him only so far; they left him and he saw them no more. He was left alone at the edge of the heaven, afraid, and fell on his face, saying to himself, 'Woe is me! What has happened to me?'",
  "gnostic.2en.21.3":
    "Enoch says that the Lord sent one of his glorious archangels, Gabriel, who told him to take heart and not be afraid, to stand up and come with him, and to stand before the Lord for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.21.4":
    "Enoch says that he answered: 'O Lord, my spirit has left me for fear and trembling! Call the men who brought me here: I have relied on them, and I would go with them before the Lord.'",
  "gnostic.2en.21.5": "Enoch says that Gabriel swept him away like a leaf carried off by the wind and set him before the face of the Lord.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXII
  "gnostic.2en.22.4": "Enoch says that he fell down and worshipped the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.22.5": "Enoch says that the Lord spoke to him with his own lips: 'Take heart, Enoch, do not be afraid; rise and stand before my face for ever.'",
  "gnostic.2en.22.6":
    "Enoch says that Michael, the chief captain, lifted him up and brought him before the Lord, and the Lord, testing his servants, said to them: 'Let Enoch come and stand before my face for ever!'",
  "gnostic.2en.22.7": "Enoch says that the glorious ones bowed down to the Lord and said, 'Let Enoch go forward as you have said!'",
  "gnostic.2en.22.8": "Enoch says that the Lord told Michael to take off Enoch's earthly robe, anoint him with the Lord's holy oil, and clothe him in the garments of the Lord's glory.",
  "gnostic.2en.22.9":
    "Enoch says that Michael did so: he anointed him and clothed him. The oil looked brighter than a great light; its anointing was like fine dew, its fragrance like myrrh, and it shone like a ray of the sun.",
  "gnostic.2en.22.10": "Enoch says that he looked at himself and he was like one of the Lord's glorious ones, with no difference, and his fear and trembling left him.",
  "gnostic.2en.22.11": "Enoch says that the Lord called one of his archangels, named Vretil, wiser than the other archangels, who wrote down all the Lord's doings.",
  "gnostic.2en.22.12":
    "Enoch says that the Lord told Vretil to bring the books out of his storehouses, give Enoch a reed pen, and explain the books to him; Vretil hurried and brought him the books, fragrant with myrrh, and gave him a reed from his own hand.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXIII
  "gnostic.2en.23.1":
    "Enoch says that Vretil told him all the works of heaven, earth and sea, their goings and comings, the noise of thunder, the sun and moon, the movement and changes of the stars, the seasons, years, days and hours, the movements of the winds, the numbers of the angels and the songs of the armed hosts,",
  "gnostic.2en.23.2":
    "Enoch goes on: and everything to do with man, every language of their songs, the lives of men, the commandments and instructions, sweet-voiced singing, and everything it is right to be taught.",
  "gnostic.2en.23.3": "Enoch says that Vretil taught him for thirty days and thirty nights without ever stopping speaking, and he wrote down everything for thirty days and thirty nights without stopping.",
  "gnostic.2en.23.4":
    "Enoch says that Vretil told him: 'You have written down all I have told you. Sit down and write about the souls of men, those not yet born, and the places prepared for them for ever,",
  "gnostic.2en.23.5": "Enoch goes on with Vretil's words: 'for every soul was created for eternity before the world was founded.'",
  "gnostic.2en.23.6": "Enoch says that he wrote it all out without a break for thirty days and thirty nights, copied it all accurately, and wrote 366 books.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXIV
  "gnostic.2en.24.1": "Enoch says that the Lord called him and told him to sit at his left hand with Gabriel, and he bowed down to the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.24.2":
    "The Lord says to Enoch that the things Enoch sees, at rest and in motion, were completed by him, and that he will now tell him from the very beginning what he created from nothing, and what visible things he made from the invisible.",
  "gnostic.2en.24.3": "The Lord says that he has not told his secrets even to his angels, nor told them how they came to be, nor have they understood his endless creation, which he is telling Enoch today.",
  "gnostic.2en.24.4": "The Lord says that before anything visible existed, he alone moved among the invisible things, like the sun going from east to west and from west to east.",
  "gnostic.2en.24.5": "The Lord says that even the sun has rest in himself, but he found no rest, because he was creating everything; and he planned to lay the foundations and make the visible creation.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXV
  "gnostic.2en.25.1": "The Lord says that he commanded in the depths that visible things should come out of the invisible, and out came Adoil, very great; he looked at him, and his colour was red, very bright.",
  "gnostic.2en.25.2": "The Lord says that he told Adoil to burst apart and let what comes out of him be seen.",
  "gnostic.2en.25.3":
    "The Lord says that Adoil burst apart and a great light came out, and he himself was in the middle of the great light; and as light came out of light, the great world came out, showing all the creation he had meant to make, and he saw that it was good.",
  "gnostic.2en.25.4": "The Lord says that he made himself a throne and sat on it, and told the light to go up on high, be set above his throne, and be the foundation of the things on high.",
  "gnostic.2en.25.5": "The Lord says that there was nothing higher than the light, and as he reclined he saw it from his throne.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXVI
  "gnostic.2en.26.1": "The Lord says that he called a second time from the depths for the solid, visible thing to come out of the invisible, and Arkhas came out, firm, heavy and very red.",
  "gnostic.2en.26.2": "The Lord says that he told Arkhas to divide and let what came from him be seen; when Arkhas divided, the world came out, very dark and great, bringing the creation of all the things below.",
  "gnostic.2en.26.3":
    "The Lord says that he saw it was good, and told it to go down, be set firm, and be the foundation of the things below; and so it was. There was nothing else below the darkness.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXVII
  "gnostic.2en.27.1": "The Lord says that he ordered the light and the darkness to be separated, and commanded a thick substance to be, and it was.",
  "gnostic.2en.27.2": "The Lord says that he spread it out and it became water, and he spread it over the darkness, below the light.",
  "gnostic.2en.27.3":
    "The Lord says that he made the waters, the depths, firm and surrounded them with light; he created seven circles and shaped them like crystal, wet and dry, like glass and ice; and he showed the waters and the other elements their paths, and showed the seven stars how each should go in its own heaven; and he saw that it was good.",
  "gnostic.2en.27.4":
    "The Lord says that he separated the light from the darkness, that is, the waters here from the waters there, and called the light day and the darkness night; and evening and morning were the first day.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXVIII
  "gnostic.2en.28.1": "The Lord says that he made the circles of the heavens firm, gathered the waters under the heavens into one place, and made the waves dry up; and so it was.",
  "gnostic.2en.28.2": "The Lord says that out of the waves he made great, firm stones, heaped up a dry substance from the stones, and called it earth.",
  "gnostic.2en.28.3": "The Lord says that in the middle of the earth he set a pit, an abyss.",
  "gnostic.2en.28.4":
    "The Lord says that he gathered the sea into one place and held it with a yoke, telling it that it had an eternal portion and must not move from its place; so he fastened the firmament and fixed it above the water.",
  "gnostic.2en.28.5": "The Lord says that he called this the first day of creation; then came evening and morning again, the second day.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXIX
  "gnostic.2en.29.1":
    "The Lord says that he made all the heavenly hosts of a fiery nature; his eye looked at the very hard stone, and from the brightness of his eye the lightning got its wonderful nature.",
  "gnostic.2en.29.2": "The Lord says that fire is in water and water in fire, and neither puts out nor dries up the other; so lightning is brighter than the sun, and soft water stronger than hard stone.",
  "gnostic.2en.29.3":
    "The Lord says that from the stone he cut out the mighty fire, and from the fire he made the ranks of the spiritual hosts, ten thousand angels, with fiery weapons and garments of burning flame, and ordered each to stand in its rank.",
  "gnostic.2en.29.4":
    "The Lord says that one of these, in the ranks of the archangels, turned away with the rank under him and conceived an impossible idea: to set his throne higher than the clouds over the earth and be equal in rank to the Lord's power.",
  "gnostic.2en.29.5": "The Lord says that he hurled him from the heights with his angels, and he was left flying in the air all the time, above the abyss.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXX
  "gnostic.2en.30.1":
    "The Lord says that so he created all the heavens, and it was the third day; on the third day he ordered the earth to bring forth great fruit trees, mountains, every kind of plant and every seed that is sown, and he planted Paradise, fenced it, set armed fiery angels to guard it, and so made a renewal.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.2": "The Lord says that then came evening and morning, the fourth day, and on the fourth day he ordered great lights to be in the circles of the heavens.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.3":
    "The Lord says that in the first and highest circle he put the star Kruno; in the second, Aphrodite; in the third, Ares; in the fourth, the Sun; in the fifth, Zeus; in the sixth, Hermes; and in the seventh, the moon.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.4": "The Lord says that he decorated the lower air with the lesser stars.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.5": "The Lord says that he set the sun to light the day and the moon and stars to light the night, the sun to go through each sign of the Zodiac, and the moon through the twelve signs.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.6": "The Lord says that he fixed their names and their being, the thunders, and how the hours turn round.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.7":
    "The Lord says that then came evening and morning, the fifth day; on the fifth day he commanded the sea to bring forth fish and every kind of winged bird, and everything that creeps on the earth, four-footed animals that go about the earth and things that fly in the air, male and female, and every living, breathing thing.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.8":
    "The Lord says that it was evening and morning, the sixth day; on the sixth day he ordered his Wisdom to make man from seven substances: his flesh from the earth, his blood from the dew, his eyes from the sun, his bones from the stones, his thoughts from the swiftness of the angels and the clouds, his veins and hair from the grass of the earth, and his spirit from the Lord's spirit and the wind.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.9": "The Lord says that he gave man seven natures: hearing to the body, sight to the eyes, smell to the perception, touch to the veins, taste to the blood, the bones for endurance, and sweetness for thought.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.10":
    "The Lord says that he planned a subtle thing: he made man from both the invisible and the visible nature; from both come his death, his life and his form; and the word was like a deed, small in something great and great in something small.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.11": "The Lord says that he set man on the earth like a second angel, honoured, great and glorious.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.12": "The Lord says that he made man a ruler to rule the earth and to have his wisdom, and that among all his creatures there was no one on earth like him.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.13": "The Lord says that he gave man a name from the four substances: east, west, north and south.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.14": "The Lord says that he appointed four special stars for him, and gave him the name Adam.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.15":
    "The Lord says that he gave Adam his own will and showed him the two ways, light and darkness, telling him which was good and which evil, so that the Lord might know whether he loved or hated him, and that among his kind he should be seen to love him.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.16": "The Lord says that he knew Adam's nature but Adam did not know it, so his ignorance is a misfortune to him that leads him to sin; and the Lord appointed death because of his sin.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.17": "The Lord says that he put Adam to sleep, took a rib from him, and made him a wife.",
  "gnostic.2en.30.18": "The Lord says that death came through Adam's wife; he received Adam's last word, and called her by a name, the mother, that is, Eve.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXI
  "gnostic.2en.31.1": "The Lord says that Adam had a life on earth (the text has a gap here), and that he made a garden in Eden in the east and ordained that Adam should keep the law and the instruction.",
  "gnostic.2en.31.2": "The Lord says that he opened the heavens for Adam so that he could see the angels singing the song of triumph, and in Paradise there was light without any darkness, always.",
  "gnostic.2en.31.3": "The Lord says that the devil schemed, as if he wanted to make another world, because things on earth were subject to Adam, for him to rule and be lord over.",
  "gnostic.2en.31.4": "The Lord says that the devil is to be the evil spirit of the lowest places; he became Satan after he left the heavens, and his name was formerly Satanail.",
  "gnostic.2en.31.5":
    "The Lord says that though Satan became different in nature from the angels, his understanding of right and sinful thoughts did not change; he understood the judgement on him and the sin he had committed before.",
  "gnostic.2en.31.6": "The Lord says that for this reason Satan made plans against Adam: he came in and deceived Eve, but he did not touch Adam.",
  "gnostic.2en.31.7": "The Lord says that he cursed Satan for his ignorance, but did not curse those he had blessed before,",
  "gnostic.2en.31.8": "The Lord goes on: he did not curse man, the earth or any other creature, but only man's evil fruit and then his works.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXII
  "gnostic.2en.32.1":
    "The Lord says that he told Adam: 'You are earth, and to the earth you came from you will return. I will not destroy you, but send you back where I took you from, and then I can take you again at my second coming.' And the Lord blessed all his creation, visible and invisible.",
  "gnostic.2en.32.2": "The Lord says that he blessed the seventh day, the Sabbath, because on it he rested from all his work.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXIII
  "gnostic.2en.33.1": "The Lord says that he also established the eighth day: the eighth is to be the first after his work, and the days are to go after the pattern of seven thousand.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.2": "The Lord says that at the beginning of the eighth thousand there is to be a time without reckoning and without end: no years, months, weeks, days or hours.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.3":
    "The Lord tells Enoch that everything he has told him and Enoch has understood, everything he has seen in heaven and on earth, and everything he has written in books, the Lord devised by his wisdom in order to create it, and made it all from the highest foundation to the lowest and to the end.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.4":
    "The Lord says that he has no counsellor and no heir to his works: he is the eternal one, not made with hands; his thought does not change, his wisdom is his counsellor and his word is reality; his eyes see all things, and if he looks at them they stand firm, but if he turns his face away, all are in need of him.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.5": "The Lord tells Enoch to pay attention and know who is speaking to him, and to take the books he has written himself.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.6":
    "The Lord says that he gives Enoch Samuil and Raguil, who brought him up, and tells him to go with them to the earth and tell his sons what the Lord has said and what Enoch has seen, from the lowest heaven up to the throne.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.7": "The Lord says that he created all the hosts and powers, and no one opposes or disobeys him: all obey his power alone and work for his rule alone.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.8": "The Lord tells Enoch to give his sons the works he has written, so that they will read them, know the Lord as Creator of all, and understand that there is no other God besides him.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.9": "The Lord says that they are to pass the books on to their children's children, from generation to generation and from nation to nation.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.10":
    "The Lord says that he will give Enoch his messenger, the great captain Michael, for his writings and those of his fathers, Adam, Seth, Enos, Kainan, Malaleel and Jared, Enoch's father.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.11": "The Lord says that he will not require the writings until the last age, for he has told his two angels, Ariukh and Pariukh, whom he has set on the earth as their guardians.",
  "gnostic.2en.33.12": "The Lord says that he has ordered them to guard the writings in due time, so that the account of what he will do in Enoch's family is not lost in the coming flood.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXIV
  "gnostic.2en.34.1":
    "The Lord says that he knows the wickedness of men: they will not bear the yoke he has put on them or sow the seed he has given them, but will throw off his yoke and take another, sow worthless seed, bow to empty gods, and deny him, the only God.",
  "gnostic.2en.34.2": "The Lord says that they will fill the whole world with wickedness and lawlessness and foul impurity with one another, sodomy and other impure practices too foul to speak of.",
  "gnostic.2en.34.3": "The Lord says that for this he will bring a flood on the earth and destroy everything, and the earth will be destroyed in great corruption.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXV
  "gnostic.2en.35.1":
    "The Lord says that he will leave a righteous man of Enoch's race, with all his house, who will do his will; from their descendants, after a time, a large generation will arise, but many of them will be very greedy.",
  "gnostic.2en.35.2":
    "The Lord says that when that family dies out, he will show them the books of Enoch's writings and of his fathers, and their guardians on earth will show them to men who are true and please him and do not take his name in vain.",
  "gnostic.2en.35.3": "The Lord says that they will tell another generation, and those who have read the books will in the end be glorified more than before.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXVI
  "gnostic.2en.36.1":
    "The Lord gives Enoch thirty days to work in his house: to tell his sons and his household, so that they listen to him, read and understand that there is no other God but the Lord, always keep his commandments, and begin to read and understand the books Enoch has written.",
  "gnostic.2en.36.2": "The Lord says that after thirty days he will send his angels for Enoch, and they will take him from the earth and from his sons, as the Lord wills.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXVII
  "gnostic.2en.37.1":
    "Enoch says (in a chapter Charles prints all in square brackets) that God called one of his greatest angels, terrible and awesome, and set him beside Enoch; the angel looked like snow, his hands were like ice and he looked very cold, and Enoch's face was chilled, because he could not bear the fear of the Lord, just as no one can bear the mighty fire and heat of the sun or the frost of the air.",
  "gnostic.2en.37.2": "Enoch says (still within the square brackets) that the Lord told him that if his face were not chilled here, no man could look at it.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXVIII
  "gnostic.2en.38.1": "Enoch says that the Lord told the men who first took him to take him back to earth with them and wait for him until the appointed day.",
  "gnostic.2en.38.2": "Enoch says that at night they laid him on his bed, where Mathusal, waiting day and night for him to come, was keeping guard.",
  "gnostic.2en.38.3": "Enoch says that Mathusal was terrified when he heard him come, and Enoch told him to call all the household so that he could tell them everything.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XXXIX
  "gnostic.2en.39.1": "Enoch says to his children that he has been sent to them today to tell them from the Lord's lips what has been, what is happening now and what will be before the day of judgement.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.2": "Enoch says that he does not speak to them from his own lips but from the lips of the Lord who sent him; they hear the words of his lips, a mortal man like themselves.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.3": "Enoch says that he has seen the face of the Lord like iron heated in the fire, which throws out sparks and burns when it is drawn out.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.4": "Enoch tells them to look at his eyes, the eyes of a man who carries a sign for them; he has seen the eyes of the Lord shining like the sun's rays and terrifying human eyes.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.5": "Enoch says that they see the right hand of a man like themselves helping them; he has seen the right hand of the Lord helping him and filling the heavens.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.6": "Enoch says that they see the scope of his actions, which is like their own; he has seen the immeasurable and harmonious form of the Lord, which has no end.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.7": "Enoch says that they hear the words of his lips, but he has heard the words of the Lord, like great thunder with the clouds in constant turmoil.",
  "gnostic.2en.39.8":
    "Enoch tells his children to listen to their earthly father: it is terrible and awesome to stand before an earthly prince, because his will is death and his will is life; how much more terrible to stand before the Lord of lords and of the earthly and heavenly hosts. Who can bear that endless terror?",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XL
  "gnostic.2en.40.1": "Enoch says that he knows all things from the Lord's lips, for his eyes have seen from the beginning to the end.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.2":
    "Enoch says that he knows everything and has written everything in the books: the heavens, their end and their fullness, all the hosts; he has measured their courses and written down the stars and their countless number.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.3": "Enoch asks what man has seen the stars' changes and courses: not even the angels know their number, but he has written down all their names.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.4": "Enoch says that he has measured the sun's circle and his rays, his coming in and going out through all the months, and all his courses, and written down their names.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.5": "Enoch says that he has measured the moon's circle, her daily waning, and the secret places where she hides each day and rises according to all the hours.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.6":
    "Enoch says that he has set down the four seasons, made four circles from them and placed the years in the circles, and the months, and reckoned the days from the months and the hours from the days.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.7":
    "Enoch says that he has written down everything that moves on the earth and everything that is fed, every seed sown and unsown that grows on the earth, everything in the garden, every plant and flower, their scents and their names.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.8": "Enoch says that he investigated the dwellings of the clouds, their shapes and wings, and how they bring rain and raindrops.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.9":
    "Enoch says that he wrote down the course of thunder and lightning, and was shown their keys, their guardians and the path they go by: they are brought out in bonds, in measure, and let go in bonds, so that their heavy force should not overload the clouds of wrath and destroy everything on earth.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.10":
    "Enoch says that he wrote down the storehouses of snow and hail and the cool breezes, and watched the keeper of their keys in the season, how he fills the clouds from them without emptying the stores.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.11":
    "Enoch says that he wrote down where the winds live, and saw how those who hold their keys carry scales and measures: first they weigh them, then let them out in measure, carefully, over the whole earth, so that their heavy breath does not shake it.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.12":
    "Enoch says that he has measured the whole earth, its mountains, hills, fields, trees, stones and rivers, written down everything that exists, the height from the earth to the seventh heaven and the depth down to the lowest hell, the place of judgement and the great hell laid open, full of lamentation; and he saw how the prisoners suffer, waiting for the boundless judgement.",
  "gnostic.2en.40.13": "Enoch says that he wrote out all those being judged by the judge, every judgement they receive, and all their deeds.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLI
  "gnostic.2en.41.1": "Enoch says that he saw all their forefathers from the beginning, with Adam and Eve, and sighed and wept and spoke of the ruin their wickedness caused: 'Woe is me for my weakness and that of my forefathers!'",
  "gnostic.2en.41.2":
    "Enoch says that he thought in his heart: 'Blessed is the man who was not born, or who, once born, never sinned before the Lord, so that he should not come to this place and bear its yoke!'",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLII
  "gnostic.2en.42.1":
    "Enoch says that he saw those who keep the keys and guard the gates of hell, standing like great serpents, their faces like lamps gone out, their eyes fiery, their teeth sharp, and stripped to the waist.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.2":
    "Enoch says that he told them to their faces that he wished he had never seen them or heard of their doings, and that his race had never come to them: 'Now they have sinned only a little in this life, and they suffer for ever in the eternal life.'",
  "gnostic.2en.42.3": "Enoch says that he went out to the east, to the Paradise of Eden, where rest is prepared for the just; it is open to the third heaven and shut off from this world.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.4": "Enoch says that guards are set at the very great gates of the east of the sun, fiery angels singing songs of triumph, who never stop rejoicing in the presence of the just.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.5":
    "Enoch says that at the last coming they will lead Adam out with their forefathers and bring them there to rejoice, as a man invites those he loves to feast with him, and they come with joy and talk in front of his house, waiting joyfully for his feast, for delight, boundless wealth, joy and merriment in the light, and eternal life.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.6":
    "Enoch tells his children: blessed is he who fears the Lord's name, serves before him always, brings his gifts with fear all his life, lives justly all his life, and dies.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.7": "Enoch says: blessed is he who judges justly, not for reward but for the sake of righteousness, expecting nothing back; a sincere judgement will come to him afterwards.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.8": "Enoch says: blessed is he who clothes the naked and gives his bread to the hungry.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.9": "Enoch says: blessed is he who judges justly for the orphan and the widow and helps everyone who is wronged.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.10": "Enoch says: blessed is he who turns from the unsteady path of this empty world and walks the right path that leads to eternal life.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.11": "Enoch says: blessed is he who sows just seed; he will reap sevenfold.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.12": "Enoch says: blessed is he in whom the truth is, so that he speaks the truth to his neighbour.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.13": "Enoch says: blessed is he who has love on his lips and tenderness in his heart.",
  "gnostic.2en.42.14":
    "Enoch says: blessed is he who understands every work of the Lord and glorifies him; for the Lord's works are just, while of man's works some are good and some evil, and people are known by their works.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLIII
  "gnostic.2en.43.1":
    "Enoch tells his children that he has written down, winter and summer, what he has learned on earth and thought over from the Lord; he has put together an account of everything, reckoned every hour of the years, measured the hours, listed them and found out all their differences.",
  "gnostic.2en.43.2":
    "Enoch says that as one year is more honoured than another, so one man is more honoured than another: one for wealth, another for wisdom of heart, understanding, cunning, keeping silent, purity, strength, good looks, youth, sharpness of mind, keen sight, or knowing many things.",
  "gnostic.2en.43.3": "Enoch says: let it be heard everywhere that no one is greater than he who fears God; he will be the most glorious for ever.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLIV
  "gnostic.2en.44.1": "Enoch says that God made man with his own hands in the likeness of his face, both small and great; whoever reviles a man's face reviles the face of the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.44.2": "Enoch says that whoever is angry with another without being wronged will be consumed by the great anger of the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.44.3": "Enoch says that a man who spits in another's face to insult him will be consumed in the Lord's great judgement.",
  "gnostic.2en.44.4":
    "Enoch says: blessed is the man who bears no malice against anyone, who helps the man who is wronged and under judgement, lifts up the oppressed, and does what is asked of him.",
  "gnostic.2en.44.5":
    "Enoch says that on the day of the great judgement every measure, standard and weight used in trade, whatever hangs on the scales, will know its own measure and be rewarded by measure.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLV
  "gnostic.2en.45.1": "Enoch says that whoever hurries to bring his offering before the Lord, the Lord will hurry to complete his work and judge justly for him.",
  "gnostic.2en.45.2": "Enoch says that whoever increases his lamp before the Lord, the Lord will greatly increase his treasure in the heavenly kingdom.",
  "gnostic.2en.45.3": "Enoch says that God does not need bread, or a light, or an animal, or any other sacrifice: these are nothing to him.",
  "gnostic.2en.45.4": "Enoch says that God requires a pure heart, and by all these things he tests the heart of man.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLVI
  "gnostic.2en.46.1":
    "Enoch tells his people to listen: if someone brings gifts to an earthly prince with unfaithfulness in his heart, and the prince knows it, will he not be angry, refuse the gifts and hand the man over to be condemned?",
  "gnostic.2en.46.2": "Enoch says that if a man flatters another with words but plans evil against him in his heart, the other will see through it, and the flatterer will be condemned, his wrongdoing plain to all.",
  "gnostic.2en.46.3": "Enoch says that when God sends a great light, by it the just and the unjust will be judged, and nothing will be hidden.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLVII
  "gnostic.2en.47.1": "Enoch tells his children to take his thoughts to heart and listen to the words of their father, which have come to them from the Lord's mouth.",
  "gnostic.2en.47.2":
    "Enoch tells them to take and read the books their father has written, in which they will learn all the Lord's works: there have been many books since the beginning and will be until the end of the world, but none will teach them as his do.",
  "gnostic.2en.47.3": "Enoch says that if they keep his writings they will not sin against God, for there is no other besides the Lord, in heaven, on earth, in the depths below or in the lonely foundations.",
  "gnostic.2en.47.4":
    "Enoch says that God laid the foundations on unknown things, stretched out the visible and invisible heavens, made the earth firm on the waters, and set the waters on things that are not fixed. Who created all the countless works of creation?",
  "gnostic.2en.47.5":
    "Enoch asks who has counted the dust of the earth, the sand of the sea, the raindrops, the morning dew and the breath of the wind; who has bound earth and sea with unbreakable bonds, cut the stars out of fire, adorned the heavens and set the sun among them so that... (the sentence breaks off as printed).",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLVIII
  "gnostic.2en.48.1": "Enoch says that the sun goes through the seven circles of the heavens, and was given 182 thrones for when he goes on a short day and 182 for when he goes on a long day.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.2":
    "Enoch says that the sun has two great thrones where he rests, turning this way and that above the monthly thrones: from the month Tsivan, after seventeen days, he goes down to the month Thevan, and from the seventeenth day of Thevad (so spelled here) he goes up.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.3":
    "Enoch says that so the sun goes through all the courses of heaven: when he comes near the earth, the earth rejoices and bears fruit; when he goes away, the earth is sad, and the trees and fruits do not grow.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.4": "Enoch says that God arranged all this by his wisdom, by measure and exact division of time, for things visible and invisible.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.5": "Enoch says that God made all visible things out of invisible ones, being himself invisible.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.6": "Enoch tells his children to hand the books on to their children, in all their families and among the nations.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.7": "Enoch says that the wise should fear God, receive the books, love them more than any food, and read them.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.8": "Enoch says that the foolish, who do not think of the Lord or fear God, will not receive the books but turn away and keep clear of them, and the terrible judgement awaits them.",
  "gnostic.2en.48.9": "Enoch says: blessed is the man who takes up their yoke and wears it, for he will be set free on the day of the great judgement.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- XLIX
  "gnostic.2en.49.1":
    "Enoch tells his children that he swears to them, yet will not swear any oath, by heaven or earth or anything else God made. God said: 'There is no swearing in me, nor injustice, but truth.' If there is no truth in men, let them swear by a word: yes, yes, or no, no.",
  "gnostic.2en.49.2":
    "Enoch says that he swears to them, yes, yes, that no man has ever been in his mother's womb without a place being prepared there for every soul, and a measure fixed for how long a man is to be tested in this world; they must not be deceived: a place is prepared there for every human soul.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- L
  "gnostic.2en.50.1": "Enoch says that he has set down in the writings what every man does; no one born on earth can hide himself or his deeds: 'I see all.'",
  "gnostic.2en.50.2": "Enoch tells his children to live out their days with patience and gentleness, and they will inherit the endless life to come.",
  "gnostic.2en.50.3": "Enoch tells them to bear every wound, affliction, evil word and attack for the Lord's sake.",
  "gnostic.2en.50.4": "Enoch tells them not to repay, even when they could take revenge, on neighbour or enemy: God will avenge them on the day of the great judgement; vengeance is not theirs to take.",
  "gnostic.2en.50.5": "Enoch says that whoever spends gold or silver for a brother will receive great treasure on the day of judgement, and tells them to reach out to the orphan, the widow and the stranger.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LI
  "gnostic.2en.51.1": "Enoch tells his children to reach out to the poor as far as they are able.",
  "gnostic.2en.51.2": "Enoch tells them not to hide their silver in the ground but to help the honest man in trouble, and trouble will not come on them when they are toiling.",
  "gnostic.2en.51.3": "Enoch tells them to bear any harsh and heavy yoke put on them for the Lord's sake, and so they will be rewarded on the day of judgement.",
  "gnostic.2en.51.4": "Enoch says that it is good to go into the house of the Lord morning, noon and evening to glorify the Creator of all.",
  "gnostic.2en.51.5": "Enoch says that therefore everything that breathes should glorify him, and every creature, visible and invisible, should praise him.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LII
  "gnostic.2en.52.1": "Enoch says: blessed is the man who opens his lips to praise the God of Sabaoth and praises the Lord with his heart.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.2": "Enoch says: cursed is every man who opens his lips to abuse and slander his neighbour.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.3": "Enoch says: blessed is he who opens his lips to bless and praise God.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.4": "Enoch says: cursed is he who opens his lips to swear and blaspheme before the Lord all his days.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.5": "Enoch says: blessed is he who blesses all the Lord's works.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.6": "Enoch says: cursed is he who speaks ill of the Lord's works.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.7": "Enoch says: blessed is he who looks to work with his own hand.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.8": "Enoch says: cursed is he who looks to live off another man's work.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.9": "Enoch says: blessed is he who keeps the foundations of his fathers from the beginning.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.10": "Enoch says: cursed is he who breaks the rules of his fathers.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.11": "Enoch says: blessed is he who makes peace and love.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.12": "Enoch says: cursed is he who troubles those who are at peace.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.13": "Enoch says: blessed is he who does not speak of peace with his tongue but has peace in his heart for all.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.14": "Enoch says: cursed is he who speaks of peace with his tongue but has no peace in his heart.",
  "gnostic.2en.52.15": "Enoch says that all these things will be revealed, in measures and in books, on the day of the great judgement.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LIII
  "gnostic.2en.53.1": "Enoch tells his children not to say that their father stands before God and prays for them to be released from sin: there is no one there to help any man who has sinned.",
  "gnostic.2en.53.2": "Enoch says that they see how he has written down the works of every man before he was created, as is done for all men for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.53.3": "Enoch says that no one can add to or take back what he has written with his own hand, for God sees everything, even the thoughts of wicked men that lie in the storerooms of the heart.",
  "gnostic.2en.53.4":
    "Enoch tells his children to pay attention to all their father's words, so that they will not be sorry later and say that their father never told them, in this time of folly.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LIV
  "gnostic.2en.54.1":
    "Enoch tells his children to let these books he has given them be the inheritance of their peace: not to hide them, but to tell them to everyone who wants them and urge them to know the Lord's very wonderful works.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LV
  "gnostic.2en.55.1": "Enoch tells his children that the appointed day and time have come near and press him to leave; the angels will come and stand before him on the earth, waiting for what they have been ordered.",
  "gnostic.2en.55.2": "Enoch says that in the morning he will go up to the highest heaven, to his eternal home.",
  "gnostic.2en.55.3": "Enoch tells them therefore to do everything that is good before the Lord.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LVI
  "gnostic.2en.56.1":
    "The narrator says that Methosalem answered his father Enoch, asking whether he might set food before him, so that, having blessed their houses, his sons and all his family, he might let his people be glorified by him, and then leave as God had said.",
  "gnostic.2en.56.2":
    "The narrator says that Enoch answered Methosalem that since God anointed him with the oil of his glory there has been no food in him, his soul remembers no earthly pleasure, and he wants nothing earthly.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LVII
  "gnostic.2en.57.1": "The narrator says that Enoch told Methosalem to call all his brothers, all their families and the elders of the people, so that he might speak to them and leave as was appointed for him.",
  "gnostic.2en.57.2":
    "The narrator says that Methosalem hurried and called his brothers, Regim, Riman, Ukhan, Khermion and Gaidal (the name in square brackets), and the elders of the people, and brought them all before Enoch, who blessed them and spoke to them.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LVIII
  "gnostic.2en.58.1": "Enoch tells his sons to listen: in the days when the Lord came on the earth for Adam's sake and visited all his creation, which he had made himself,",
  "gnostic.2en.58.2": "Enoch goes on: the Lord called all the cattle of the earth, all creeping things and all the birds of the air, and brought them before their father Adam, and Adam named every living thing on earth.",
  "gnostic.2en.58.3": "Enoch says that the Lord made Adam lord over everything, put everything under his hands and made it submit and obey man: so the Lord created man as master of all his possessions.",
  "gnostic.2en.58.4": "Enoch says that the Lord will not judge any beast's soul because of man, but he will judge man's soul because of the souls of beasts in the world to come.",
  "gnostic.2en.58.5":
    "Enoch says that just as there is a special place for all the souls of men according to their number, so there is for beasts; and not one soul God has made will perish before the great judgement.",
  "gnostic.2en.58.6": "Enoch says that every beast's soul will accuse man if he feeds it badly.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LIX
  "gnostic.2en.59.1": "Enoch says that whoever acts lawlessly towards the souls of beasts acts lawlessly towards his own soul.",
  "gnostic.2en.59.2": "Enoch says that a man offers clean animals and makes his sacrifice to preserve his soul; if he offers clean beasts and birds in sacrifice, he preserves his soul.",
  "gnostic.2en.59.3": "Enoch says that whatever is given them for food they should bind by the four feet: that is an atonement; so a man acts rightly and preserves his soul.",
  "gnostic.2en.59.4": "Enoch says that whoever kills a beast without a wound kills his own soul and sins against his own flesh.",
  "gnostic.2en.59.5": "Enoch says that whoever harms an animal in secret follows an evil custom and sins against his own soul.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LX
  "gnostic.2en.60.1": "Enoch says that whoever harms the soul of a man harms his own soul, and there is no salvation or forgiveness for his flesh for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.60.2": "Enoch says that whoever kills the soul of a man kills his own soul and destroys his own body, and there is no salvation for him for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.60.3": "Enoch says that whoever sets a net for another man will fall into it himself, and there is no salvation for him for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.60.4": "Enoch says that whoever prepares a weapon against a man will not escape punishment in the great judgement for ever.",
  "gnostic.2en.60.5": "Enoch says that whoever acts crookedly or speaks evil against any soul will have no righteousness for himself for ever.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXI
  "gnostic.2en.61.1": "Enoch tells his children to keep their hearts from every wrong the Lord hates: as a man asks God for his own soul, so he should do to every living soul.",
  "gnostic.2en.61.2": "Enoch says that he knows that in the world to come there are many dwellings prepared for men, good for the good and evil for the evil, many and without number.",
  "gnostic.2en.61.3": "Enoch says: blessed are those who go to the dwellings of the blessed, for in the evil ones there is no rest and no way back.",
  "gnostic.2en.61.4":
    "Enoch tells them, small and great, that when a man has a good thought in his heart and brings gifts of his labours before the Lord, if his own hands did not make them, the Lord turns his face away from the work of his hands and he can gain nothing from it.",
  "gnostic.2en.61.5": "Enoch says that if his hands did make them but his heart grumbles, and he does not offer his heart but keeps grumbling, he has no success.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXII
  "gnostic.2en.62.1": "Enoch says: blessed is the man who patiently brings his gifts before the Lord, for he will turn aside the punishment of his sin.",
  "gnostic.2en.62.2":
    "Enoch says that if a man speaks words at the wrong time there is no repentance for him; if he lets the appointed time pass and does not do the work, he is not blessed, for there is no repentance after death.",
  "gnostic.2en.62.3": "Enoch says that every deed a man does at the wrong time is an offence before men and a sin before God.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXIII
  "gnostic.2en.63.1": "Enoch says that when a man clothes the naked and feeds the hungry, he is rewarded by God.",
  "gnostic.2en.63.2": "Enoch says that if his heart grumbles, he does himself a double harm: he ruins what he gives, and there will be no reward for it.",
  "gnostic.2en.63.3": "Enoch says that when the poor man, once his heart is satisfied or his body clothed, behaves with contempt, he destroys the worth of all his endurance of poverty and will not gain the blessing of a reward.",
  "gnostic.2en.63.4":
    "Enoch says that the Lord hates every contemptuous and boastful man, every lying word, and whatever is covered with wrongdoing: it is cut with the edge of a deadly sword, thrown into the fire, and burns for ever.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXIV
  "gnostic.2en.64.1":
    "The narrator says that when Enoch had said these words to his sons and the princes of the people, all the people, near and far, heard that the Lord was calling Enoch, and they agreed together to go and kiss him.",
  "gnostic.2en.64.2": "The narrator says that the men gathered, two thousand of them, and came to the place Achuzan, where Enoch and his sons were.",
  "gnostic.2en.64.3": "The narrator says that the elders of the people came together, bowed down, kissed Enoch, and said, 'Enoch, our father, be blessed by the Lord, the eternal King!'",
  "gnostic.2en.64.4": "The narrator goes on with the elders' words: they ask Enoch to bless his sons and all the people, so that they may be glorified before him today.",
  "gnostic.2en.64.5":
    "The narrator goes on with the elders' words: Enoch is glorified before the Lord for ever, since God has chosen him above all men on earth and made him the scribe of his creation of visible and invisible things, an avenger of men's sins and a help to his family. And Enoch answered all his people.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXV
  "gnostic.2en.65.1": "Enoch tells his children that before anything existed and all creatures were made, the Lord made all things, visible and invisible.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.2":
    "Enoch says that when the times of these things had come and gone, after all of them God made man in his own image and likeness, and gave him eyes to see, ears to hear, a heart to understand, and reason to take counsel.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.3":
    "Enoch says that the Lord looked on the world for man's sake and made all creation for him, and divided it into times: from the times he made years, from the years months, from the months days, and of the days he made seven.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.4":
    "Enoch says that in these he made the hours and divided them into small parts, so that man should understand the seasons, reckon years, months and hours, their changes, beginnings and ends, reckon his own life from beginning to death, think about his sin, and write down his evil and good deeds.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.5": "Enoch says that nothing done is hidden from the Lord; let each man know his deeds, not break the commandments, and keep 'My writings' safe from generation to generation.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.6": "Enoch says that when all the creation, visible and invisible, that the Lord has made comes to an end, every man will come to the Lord's great judgement.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.7": "Enoch says that then the times will perish: there will be no year, month or day, and no hours, and they will not be counted.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.8":
    "Enoch says that there will be one eternity, and all the just who escape the Lord's great judgement will be gathered together into eternal life, for ever and ever, and they will be eternal.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.9": "Enoch says that there will be no labour, sickness, sorrow, anxiety or want, no night and no darkness, but a great light.",
  "gnostic.2en.65.10":
    "Enoch says that they will have a great wall that cannot be broken down, and a bright, incorruptible paradise will be their protection and eternal home; for everything corruptible will pass away, and there will be eternal life.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXVI
  "gnostic.2en.66.1": "Enoch tells his children to keep their souls from every wrong the Lord hates, to walk before him in fear and trembling and serve him alone, and to worship the true God, not dumb idols.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.2": "Enoch tells them to heed the Lord's command and bring every just offering before him, for the Lord hates what is unjust.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.3": "Enoch says that the Lord sees everything: whatever a man thinks in his heart, whatever he plans, every thought is always before the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.4":
    "Enoch says that if they look at the heavens, the Lord is there, for he made the heavens; if at the earth, he is there, for he made it firm and set every creature in it; if they search the depths of the sea and everything under the earth, the Lord is there too, for he created all things.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.5": "Enoch tells them not to bow down to the work of men or even to the work of the Lord, leaving the Lord of all creation, for no deed is hidden from him.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.6":
    "Enoch tells his children to walk in patience and humility, through slander and insult, in faith and truth, in the promises and in sickness, abuse, wounds, temptation, nakedness and want, loving one another, until they leave this world of sickness; then they will inherit eternity.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.7": "Enoch says: blessed are the just who escape the great judgement! They will be seven times brighter than the sun, for in this age the seventh part of everything is set apart.",
  "gnostic.2en.66.8":
    "Enoch says that about light and darkness, food, sweet things and bitter things, paradise and torments, fires, frosts and other things, he has written it all down so that they may read and understand.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXVII
  "gnostic.2en.67.1": "The narrator says that when Enoch had spoken with the people, the Lord sent darkness on the earth, and there was gloom that hid the men standing with Enoch.",
  "gnostic.2en.67.2":
    "The narrator says that the angels hurried, took Enoch and carried him to the highest heaven, where the Lord received him and set him before his face; and the darkness left the earth, and there was light.",
  "gnostic.2en.67.3": "The narrator says that the people saw it but did not understand how Enoch was taken, and they glorified God; and those who had seen these things went home.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- LXVIII
  "gnostic.2en.68.1": "The narrator says that Enoch was born on the sixth day of the month Tsivan and lived 365 years; he was taken up to heaven on the first day of the month Tsivan and was in heaven sixty days.",
  "gnostic.2en.68.2": "The narrator says that Enoch wrote down descriptions of all the creation the Lord had made, wrote 366 books, and gave them to his sons.",
  "gnostic.2en.68.3": "The narrator says that Enoch was on earth thirty days, and was then taken to heaven in the same month Tsivan, on the same day, the sixth, the day and hour of his birth.",
  "gnostic.2en.68.4": "The narrator says that as every man's existence in this life is dark, so are his beginning, birth and departure: in the hour he began, he is born and he departs.",
  "gnostic.2en.68.5": "The narrator says that Methusalem and all his brothers, Enoch's sons, hurried and built an altar at the place called Achuzan, where and when Enoch was taken up to heaven.",
  "gnostic.2en.68.6": "The narrator says that they took cattle, invited all the people, and sacrificed victims before the Lord.",
  "gnostic.2en.68.7":
    "The narrator says that all the people and their elders, the whole crowd, came to the festival and brought gifts to Enoch's sons; they held a great festival, rejoicing and merry for three days, praising God who had given such a sign through Enoch, who had found favour with him, so that they should hand it down to their sons' sons, from generation to generation, for ever. Amen.",
};
